Mission Local asked the District 3 candidates what they thought about the situation at the Granada Hotel, a former senior SRO acquired by the city for supportive housing. They generally criticized the transition and called for better oversight and accountability. Moe Jamil said the city had concentrated too many shelters and supportive housing sites in Lower Nob Hill. Sharon Lai said the conversion was rushed and harmed legacy tenants, and that they should have been involved and offered relocation options. Eduard Navarro called the building’s condition deplorable and said SROs should not be treated as hospitals or warehouses. Danny Sauter called for zero-tolerance policies for drug use in common areas and faster safety work. Matthew Susk said the acquisition led to declines in safety and living conditions. JConr B. Ortega blamed inadequate oversight and called for the city, rather than nonprofits, to take responsibility.

